# Metric click dual-action (delivery-ops)

Extends user-level `jira-authenticity-links` §1 for this monorepo.

## Hard rule

On **every** delivery-ops page metric that can show tickets in-app:

| Control | Must do |
|---|---|
| Count / number | Open **side panel / drill** (`onOpen`, `onHeroClick`, drawer) |
| Open in JIRA ↗ | Open **exact JQL** in a new tab |

## Never

- Count and “Open in JIRA” both navigate to JIRA
- Hide the JIRA proof when `onOpen` exists (tile and/or drawer header must expose it)
- Show a redundant “Open in JIRA” hint when the count itself is already the only JIRA link (no drill)

## When wiring a new hero / chip

1. Prefer shared patterns: OnCalls `Hero`, KPI Pulse `PulseHero` + `onHeroClick`, Sprint Performance `#drill`.
2. Pass `onOpen` / `onHeroClick` whenever the API returns a row sample for that metric.
3. Document dual-click in the page’s `*-requirements.md` UI Behaviour section (`page-docs-required`).

## Review gate

Pipeline **JIRA Query Checker** and **UX** stages fail the change if a metric with an in-app sample still sends the count externally only.
